  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`Autocomplete` provides user a list of suggestions based on the input,\nhowever user is not limited to suggestions and can type anything.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled",
      "text": "`Autocomplete` value must be a string, other types are not supported.\n`onChange` function is called with a string value as a single argument.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sort options",
      "text": "By default, options are sorted by their position in the data array. You can change this behavior\nwith `filter` function:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "renderOption",
      "text": "`renderOption` callback allows you to customize option rendering. It is called with option object.\nThe function must return a React node.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scrollable dropdown",
      "text": "By default, the options list is wrapped with [ScrollArea.Autosize](/core/scroll-area).\nYou can control dropdown max-height with `maxDropdownHeight` prop if you do not change the default settings.\n\nIf you want to use native scrollbars, set `withScrollArea={false}`. Note that in this case,\nyou will need to change dropdown styles with [Styles API](/styles/styles-api).",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled options",
      "text": "When option is disabled, it cannot be selected and is ignored in keyboard navigation.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inside Popover",
      "text": "To use `Autocomplete` inside popover, you need to set `withinPortal: false`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Clearable",
      "text": "Set `clearable` prop to display the clear button in the right section. The button is not displayed\nwhen:\n\n- The component does not have a value\n- The component is disabled\n- The component is read only",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Control dropdown opened state",
      "text": "You can control dropdown opened state with `dropdownOpened` prop. Additionally,\nyou can use `onDropdownClose` and `onDropdownOpen` to listen to dropdown opened state changes.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dropdown position",
      "text": "By default, the dropdown is displayed below the input if there is enough space; otherwise it is displayed above the input.\nYou can change this behavior by setting `position` and `middlewares` props, which are passed down to the\nunderlying [Popover](/core/popover) component.\n\nExample of dropdown that is always displayed above the input:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dropdown animation",
      "text": "By default, dropdown animations are disabled. To enable them, you can set `transitionProps`,\nwhich will be passed down to the underlying [Transition](/core/transition) component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Read only",
      "text": "Set `readOnly` to make the input read only. When `readOnly` is set,\n`Autocomplete` will not show suggestions and will not call `onChange` function.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled",
      "text": "Set `disabled` to disable the input. When `disabled` is set,\nuser cannot interact with the input and `Autocomplete` will not show suggestions.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
